Patch 3008: the tick-locked audio's output plays each tick's blocks over the time-sync-stretched tick (feed-forward; AUDIO_LOCK_FF=0 turns it off).

Symptom (test6 testers): the sound is choppy for the whole online fight, menus are fine. The time sync (port, jsp_net_game.cpp) makes each tick
period longer by (frames ahead - 0.5) ms, at most 2 ms (6%), on the peer that is ahead, but a tick still mixes 6.25 blocks (33.3 ms). The output's
rate control (patch 3007) makes up at most AUDIO_LOCK_DRC/256 (1.6%), so above about 0.5 ms per tick the device drained and a gap was concealed
every few seconds; the rate sat at its +1.56% cap in every measurement of 3007 rev 2.

Output only (blocks mixed, read index and notify events are exactly as in 3005; muted re-run blocks are never submitted, so they never see it):
- g_ps3_audio_lock_stretch_us: the stretch of the tick period that starts at this boundary in microseconds, written by the game thread before
  ps3_audio_lock_set_target (0 = none, also in the bench and with the lockstep clock off);
- the first block of a burst adds stretch / 33333 us to the resampler's rate, so the tick's blocks last as long as the stretched tick; the feedback
  (its own cap unchanged) only handles what is left. The total is capped at +-8% (a block makes at most 278 frames; LK_OUTMAX is 528);
- AUDIO_LOCK_FF (default 1; 0 = 3007 as it was, with the counters) for an A/B in one build. With AUDIO_LOCK_SMOOTH=0 there is no resampler and no
  feed-forward;
- the "[audio-lock]" line keeps every field and their order and appends: "stretch fed forward: N bursts, mean X us, max Y us, total rate a..b %,
  feed-forward on|off". The bursts and stretch are what the output saw (also with it off); "rate" stays the feedback's own, "total rate" includes it;
- tests: libs/audio/tests/test_audio_lock_race.c adds a steady 0.5, 1 and 2 ms stretch on a 150 ms fake device in virtual time, on and off (on: no
  concealed gap after the start, the level at the cushion, the feedback not pinned; off: concealed gaps) and the 8% cap; audio_lock_measure.c
  publishes each scenario's stretch as the game does and adds 1 and 2 ms scenarios, a "field hitches" scenario (76 ms about every 11 s, every
  third one 150-300 ms, as test6 matches logged them) and a scenario filter (second argument).

